  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\nThunderstorms developing in association with another impulse across \nIllinois and Missouri will move across the area this afternoon. This \nwill also be in conjunctions with a pre-frontal trough. Precipitable \nwater will still be high, but the warm cloud layer will not be quite \nas deep. So there may still be locally heavy rain, but the flooding \nthreat appears to be more isolated. In addition, with moderate \ninstability there could be some more robust storms that could produce\nstrong to damaging winds.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2)\nLow amplitude short wave will push a cold front into the area\ntonight. This will become elongated in a north northeast to south\nsouthwest orientation which will cause the boundary to be slow to\nmove all of the way through the region. There will still be some\npotential for showers and storms until this front clears. \n\nBroad long wave trough will move into the Great Lakes towards mid\nweek. This will push another cold front through late Wednesday into\nWednesday night. There will be a bigger change in air mass with highs\nwill be in the 70s with lows in the 50s to lower 60s for the latter \npart of the week.",
